			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody"><img src="http://mywebpage.netscape.com/murdockP4/iksarskel.jpg" border="0" />
<br />

<br />
	Snide clutched his chest, using that hammer always electrified his body in a strange way.  Darkness surrounded him.  He couldn’t see at all.  He had to hide before anyone from the Overthere saw him.  The only way he was able to get the hammer infused with the gate spell in the first place was by using a dark elf illusion.  Until he was able to place the illusion on again he wasn't safe.  Those in the Overthere didn't trust Barbarians at all and he would be killed on sight.
<br />
He was on a ship on the shore of the Overthere, down in the hold, beneath the deck.  Snide took out his mask of deception and placed it over his face.  The mask glowed and shimmered as it cast the illusion spell, slowly transforming him...  But Snide wasn't very lucky that day.  The light illuminated some of the lower decks so that he could see an iksar skeleton standing over some of the supplies stowed there.  The skeleton worker stood right in front of him.  It took off its skull and removed some of the maggots inside before placing it back on. Then it charged him, swinging its workers mallet for his head.  It glanced across his face, knocking off the mask and interupting the spell.  Again it was completely dark.
<br />

<br />
Cursing his Barbarian’s eyes, Snide tried as best he could to strike the bones in the darkness of the boat.  He was beneath the deck, trapped in the darkness.  His knife whistled in the air, but hit nothing.  The hits from the hammer seemed to come from all sides, he didn’t know which way to turn.  He was lucky the skeleton wasn’t a very good aim.  The hammer swung over his head and several times.  The skeleton cackled and then Snide turned to slash.  Success, he hit bones.  He slashed again but missed.  The skeleton had moved.  It cackled, and then the rogue heard footsteps above.  He reached ahead trying to find stairs or a barrel to hide behind.  Tripping over a large bag, he fell to the ground with a loud thud.  Feet pounded on the deck above and then down the stairs into the hold.
<br />

<br />
“A stowaway!  Die Barbarian!”  It must have been a dark elf, they patrolled the shores, Snide thought quickly. 
<br />

<br />
	He felt something on the deck.  It was his mask!  Shoving the mask over his face, he stood up, now able to see a little with the glowing.  He dodged the Dragoon that came at him and ran up the stairs, pushing open the hatch.  The ship was right next to the shore.  If he was lucky he could jump into the water and be rid of the people chasing him.  He locked the latch on the hold and ran to the starboard side of the ship, near the beach.  The hatch shook as the Dragoon bashed it from below.  Without delay Snide jumped off the deck and rolled across the sand as he landed.  Saltwater sprayed as he ran across the surf and dove off into the waves.  With fast paniced strokes, he had swam across the shoreline till he was on the other side of the outpost.  Determined to escape, he walked onto the beach and emptied his boots of water.  He really hated getting wet, it would take forever to get dry again.  The rogue stuck close to the wall of the outpost, approaching the book.  In the distance he saw a Cliff Golem and a dark elf exiting the gates of the outpost, near the Plane of Knowledge book.
<br />

<br />
Snide swore, and began to sprint towards the book.  He had to reach it before they cut off his escape.  Snide ran to the Book as fast as he could, but they reached it before he could.  Snide stopped.  The Golem stood in front of the book, huge and unmovable, blocking his exit.  The Dragoon made a dead run towards Snide.
<br />

<br />
With a bellow, the rogue began running again, but as they approached, Snide jumped high in the air, over the Dragoon, and as he flew over his head, the dark elf swung his sword, but far too late.  Now was the matter of the Golem.  It swung its massive fists at him, but Snide dove to the ground, and rolled underneath its massive frame, beneath its legs, and then stood to press his fingers against the pages.  As his hand pressed against the surface, he felt the golems fist swing into his back.
<br />

<br />
	Snide arrived in the Plane of Knowledge on his back and barely able to breath.  After swearing for about half an hour Snide broke the hammer over his knee.</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
