				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody"><img src="http://mywebpage.netscape.com/murdockP4/tundra.jpg" border="0" />
<br />

<br />

<br />
	A female high elf drew her hammer from the ground, and stood up.  With wide arcs she drew runes in the air and blue light flowed over Snide, and he was healed.
<br />

<br />
	“Ugh, much better.”
<br />

<br />
	“You ok?” She said with a sweet smile.
<br />

<br />
	“Yup, that bastard Dragoon W’Selo and his friend almost got me.”
<br />

<br />
	“You getting experience in the Overthere?”
<br />

<br />
	“Not in that place.  I still need to find a group.”
<br />

<br />
	“My friends and I are going to one of the Dungeons that the Wayfarers have found, would you like to come?  We need someone that can disarm traps.”
<br />

<br />
	“It’s better than nothing,” Snide said with a tired voice.
<br />

<br />
	“We are all meeting in Everfrost.  We are going to Miragul’s” She said shivering with excitement.
<br />

<br />
	“Alright. I’ll see you all there, I have to go get some rations anyway,” Snide said.
<br />

<br />
	“Ok,” she waved at him. And he simply nodded.  He ran off to the Everfrost portal, and touched the smooth surface, electric force moved through his body and he was transported to the Mountains of Everfrost.
<br />

<br />
Never feeling quite right in the cold, Snide wrapped his cloak closer about his shoulders.  Everfrost seemed so quaint to him, full of backwards Barbarians.  He almost felt sorry for them.  But when most of them hate you, hating them back is easy enough.  After sneaking past Snowflake, Snide ran across the snow.  He didn’t want the Everfrost guards chasing him.
<br />

<br />
On the way to Wayfarer camp he saw Tundra Jack and Iceberg running by.  Snide felt rage build up inside him, for this man and his blundering bear that ran over the frozen river, attacking those he thought foe, always roaming his home ‘protecting’ his home.  Snide jumped high, pushing against the frozen snow and landed on the bear’s back, burying his rage as deep into its back as he could.  The bear bellowed in pain.  As it rolled, so did Snide, but in an opposite direction over the beasts neck.  The bear batted the large rogue in the face, knocking him off his fury perch onto the snow.  And then with a snarl Iceberg rolled again, onto its paws, face to face with Snide.  The bear lunged with his massive maw, only to taste steel, as Snide’s rage entered through the inside of Iceberg’s mouth into his brain.  Then, he collapsed.
<br />

<br />
Snide was barely able to prepare himself as he saw Tundra Jack run up towards him, over a hill, his pickaxes ready to spill blood on the new snow.
<br />

<br />
“Die you thieving cur!  Go back to the Karanas,” he yelled.  Snide knew he was overmatched, so he ran towards the Wayfarer’s camp, hoping he would find refuge in the mass of adventurers there.  He was successful, for the dark elves and trolls taking rest at the camp were rudely awakened by a Barbarian that hopped over them, and then another Barbarian ran up to them, this one slashing them, rousing them from their respite.
<br />

<br />
“Outlanders begone!”  Snide smirked as the dark elves overcame Tundra Jack, and Snide helped.  Pressing the attack, Snide stabbed rage into the defeated man’s back.  The others left in victory as Tundra Jack fled, but Snide continued to goad him, until Jack fell, and the snow was soaked with his blood.</span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
