				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody"><img src="http://mywebpage.netscape.com/murdockP4/fur.jpg" border="0" />
<br />

<br />
“The one known as Snide,” the Seventh Hammer said in a deep and echoing voice.   “His crimes,” The Seventh Hammer took a scroll from his robe and opened it.  It unrolled all the way to the floor.  Snide grinned from ear to ear upon seeing the impressive list.
<br />

<br />
	He began reading, “Robbing, Looting, Destruction of Property, Smuggling, Impersonation of a Royal Priest of Prexus in order to gain access to the Temple and assassinate members of Erudite nobility, stealing in excess of 10 thousand platinum from a mentally handicap gnome in order to buy gloves, torturing an innocent, killing an innocent….”  The charges continued for about ten whole minutes.  Snide had forgotten some of them, but he nodded and smiled in recognition of his feats.
<br />

<br />
The deep booming voices of the Tribunal spoke in perfect unison, “YOUR JUDGEMENT HAS COME.”
<br />

<br />
	Snide stood dumbfounded.  What kind of silly dream this?  He chuckled.
<br />

<br />
	“THOU PAYEST HEED TO NO ONE.  THOU RESPECTETH NO ONE.  THOU ART AN OUTCAST TO ALL, SAVE THE SCANT FEW WHO THAT ART ROGUES THEMSELVES.  THOU ART A COLD BLOODED KILLER WITHOUT REMORSE.  A DOG’S DEATH IS WHAT THEE DESERVETH.  WE AUGHT TAKE YOU NOW AND DESTROY THY MORTAL FRAME.”
<br />

<br />
	“What are you talking about?” he said, swallowing his pride for a second.
<br />

<br />
	 “BECAUSE OF THE CIRCUMSTANCES OF YOUR PURPOSE IN THIS WORLD WE GIVE THEE A CHANCE FEW EVER WILL.  YOU WERE MEANT FOR MUCH GREATER THINGS IN HALAS.  THY FATE WAS TO BECOME A SHAMAN, BUT WHEN THE BANDITS OF KARANA KILLED THY PARENTS THY DESTINY WAS ALTERED.”
<br />

<br />
	Snide didn’t understand, he was about to speak again when—
<br />

<br />
	“BUT THOU HAST IGNORED RULES FOR TOO LONG, AND SO HAS SO MANY MORTALS AS OF LATE.  THEY COME TO DESTROY GODS, FOR THEIR DESIRE FOR POWER IS INSATIABLE,” they said together.  “AND BECAUSE OF THAT, THE GODS ARE LEAVING THEE.”
<br />

<br />
	“I care not for the Gods.”
<br />

<br />
	“NONETHELESS, THE RACES OF NORRATH WILL BE DEVASTATED BY THE LOSS OF THE GODS.  WITH OUR DEPARTING TERRIBLE THINGS WILL BEFALL NORRATH AND THOUSANDS OF MORTALS WILL DIE.  THE ORCS WILL REGAIN THEIR FORMER INTELLIGENCE AND COULD PLAGUE NORRATH AGAIN.  THOU CANETH CHANGE THY FATE.  THOU CANETH CHANGE THE FATE OF MANY MORTALS.  LIVE THY LIFE ACCORDING TO JUSTICE, AND INSPIRE IT IN OTHERS AND PERHAPS THOU MAY BE SPARED.”
<br />

<br />
	“Why should I care for others when they care not for me?”  Snide shouted in defiance.
<br />

<br />
	“THOU SHALT SEE THE RESULT OF THINE ACTIONS BY THE DESTRUCTION THAT FALLS UPON THE EARTH.  THOU SHALT BE SLAIN AND THOU WILT BE FORGOTTEN UNLESS THOU CHANGETH.”
<br />
Snide fell to his knees.  “How can I?  I don’t have any faith or honor left it me,” Snide said sadly.
<br />

<br />
	“LOOK INSIDE THYSELF.  WHILE OUR TIME IS YET SHORT, WE WILL BE WATCHING THEE.”
<br />

<br />
	“I know not where to start.  How can I begin a new life when I don’t know how?  I’ve never known good or evil, only the will to fight and survive.”
<br />

<br />
	“YOU MUST VISIT THE RACES OF NORRATH AND DELIVER OUR MESSAGE.  THIS IS THY SENTENCE.”
<br />

<br />
	“You must be joking.”
<br />

<br />
	“WE DO NOT MAKE JOKES.  VISIT LON IN THE TEMPLE OF RO, COMPLETE HIS QUEST, AND THEN YOU CAN BEGIN YOUR TRUE REDEMPTION.”
<br />

<br />
	Snide looked at the Tribunal dubiously.  “How do I redeem myself?”
<br />

<br />
	“GO TELL THE LEADERS OF AK’KANON, FELWITHE, KELETHIN, HALAS, NERIAK, KALADIM, ERUDIN, PAINEEL, FREEPORT, QEYNOS, RIVERVALE, CABALIS, GROBB,  SHAR VAHL, AND GUK—.”
<br />
“No, no,” Snide interrupted, although they didn’t really stop talking, he just stopped listening.  “You want me to visit places where I’m wanted dead?  That’s suicide.  Isn’t there someone else that can do this?”
<br />

<br />
“THOU SHALT NOT GO ALONE TO THE CITIES.  THOU CANEST BRING OTHERS, BUT THOU MUST TAKE OUR NEWS.  THOU AND THOU ALONE MUST BE THE ONE TO TELL THEM.  THOU SHALL HAVE COMPANY WITH THOSE THAT SPEAK OF THY FATE.”
<br />

<br />
	Snide looked up with true repentance for the first time in his life and nodded.  A small light in his soul was born in utter darkness, and Snide’s cold heart grew warm (Wonders never really did cease).
<br />

<br />
	“REMEMBER THY FATE WILL FIND YOU.  AND JUSTICE WILL BE FOUND,” the Six Hammers pounded their gavels on their hands.  Bright light glowed through the room and the Seventh hammer gestured with his gavel, pointing down.  Snide’s head suddenly seared with pain, and he fell to the ground. The room glowed with light, and it, became unbearable to his eyes as it grew brighter all around him.
<br />

<br />
