				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody"><img src="http://mywebpage.netscape.com/murdockP4/fubarz.jpg" border="0" />
<br />

<br />
Snide woke with a great pain, he was still pale and cold.  Fubarz hovered over him and was startled with Snide’s sudden sigh.
<br />

<br />
“You’re alive!  Tunare, you were dead just a few hours ago.  We were just arguing on whether to burry or burn you.”
<br />

<br />
Cemberfrost looked down at Snide with stern countenance, “I killed you.  Fubarz himself verified that fact.  But I shall make sure of it this time, to send you to the Tribunal for your crimes,”  Cemberfrost drew his sword with a ring of steel and held it over his head with both hands ready to plunge it into Snide’s chest.
<br />

<br />

<br />
	“Wait! I saw the Tribunal” He said quickly.
<br />
	
<br />
“What?!”
<br />

<br />
	“I saw them, they spoke to me.”
<br />

<br />
	“Why are you still here then, why aren’t you still imprisoned in the Plane of Justice?  Speak fast!”
<br />

<br />
	“Let me explain,” Snide said frantically, for the first time praying to the Tribunal that Cemberfrost hand would be stayed, and that he could relate his experience before he was killed again.  Snide took his time to tell both Fubarz and Cemberfrost what had happened to him, his trial before the Six Hammers, and their sentence.  When he was finished Fubarz was the first to talk.
<br />

<br />
	“You must have hit your head harder than I thought,” he put his hand over Snide’s head, intent of feeling for lumps, but Snide waved his hand away.
<br />

<br />
	“I knew you wouldn’t believe me.  It sounds crazy doesn’t it?”
<br />

<br />
	Fubarz looked at Snide doubtfully, but Cemberfrost seemed lost in thought.
<br />

<br />
	“Would the Dark Inheritance help?” Snide asked Cemberfrost.
<br />

<br />
	“Huh? Oh, uh they might, most likely those belonging to the cities you mentioned.”
<br />

<br />
	“I’ve done so many terrible things.  I was trying to survive, but there was a better way.  It may not be easier, but it is the just way.  The way of the Tribunal.  I’ve been too headstrong, and I’m sorry for it.  I know it may be too late but I wish you would forgive me for my rash actions in ShadowHaven, Cemberfrost.”
<br />

<br />
	“It takes time for us to find ourselves,” Fubarz said wisely.
<br />

<br />
	“Aye that it does,” Cemberfrost said with a stroke of his fiery red beard, “And sometimes it takes fate to find us.”
<br />

<br />
	Snide looked at Cemberfrost dubiously, tilting his head.  “What?”
<br />

<br />
	“Huh?” Cemberfrost asked.
<br />

<br />
	“Fate?”
<br />

<br />
	“Oh I was just talking,” Cemberfrost said casually.
<br />

<br />
	“No, what do you mean?” Snide asked.
<br />

<br />
	“I don’t know it, kinda just popped in my head.  I really didn’t mean anything by it.”
<br />

<br />
Fubarz breathed the cold air in slowly.  “You can change.  You don’t have to be like you were.  You can find good inside yourself.  I have seen many come from the halls of doubt and embrace goodness.”  Fubarz said with hope.
<br />

<br />
“Aye.  I will no longer be Snide.  No longer sniveling and cursed.  Well, I may always be snide, but perhaps I can change, be like Jack.  Strong and brave,” he said softly.  Raising his face to Cemberfrost, he said, “I think it is time I returned.  I need friends again to help me through this.  Hopefully when I have redeemed myself, I can be a better part of the Inheritance.”
<br />

<br />
	“I’ll tell Serrik the next time I see him, if you’d like to petition Altus Concilium to return.”
<br />

<br />
	“Yes. Good,” he said shortly.  “I need to head to the Lavastorm Mountains.  That is where my redemption begins.”
<br />

<br />
	“With Lon the Redeemed?”  Fubarz asked.
<br />

<br />
	“Aye. Where are my clothes?”
<br />

<br />
“Right here,” Cemberfrost said sofly patting a pile that was drying in front of the fire.  He took off his helmet.
<br />

<br />
	“So why don’t you say it?” He said turning towards the Barbarian warrior.
<br />

<br />
	“Hmm?” the bald but bearded Barbarian questioned.
<br />

<br />
	“That I was wrong for leaving Umbra, and that you knew you’d find me like this, unable to take care of myself.”
<br />

<br />
	Cemberfrost shook his head.  “I thought it lucky to find you, you but..”  He paused.  “I feel like fate is always using me.”
<br />

<br />
	“I would had never agreed with you until now,” Snide frowned.  Snide began to rise, but he suddenly felt very dizzy and the pain in his leg was unbearable.
<br />

<br />
	“Hold on.  You had a nasty fall, but now that your spirit has rejoined your body, I can heal you,” Fubarz said with kindness.  Quickly Fubarz drew runes in the air with his fingers, an intricate spell, taking much time, until there was an intense glow that covered his hands, then a blue glow surrounded Snide and he felt completely healed.
<br />

<br />
	 “Thank you,” Snide said slowly and with true feeling.
<br />

<br />
	The High Elf nodded at him and Snide turned towards Cemberfrost.
<br />

<br />
	“When I come back to Halas, would you help me speak to the tribes of Halas, to relate the Tribunal’s message?”
<br />

<br />
	Cemberfrost stood silent for a minute.  “Yes.”
<br />
Snide got up slowly and Cemberfrost gave him his hand, raising him onto his feet.  The rogue still felt a dull pain in his leg.  
<br />
“You healed me completely Fubarz?”
<br />

<br />
	“Yes, why?”
<br />

<br />
	“Just wondering,” he muttered, shaking his head.  The pain reminded him of his dream, and the future of which the Six Hammers spoke.  “Send me word when Altus Concilium has decided,” he said, walking along, using a Takish-Hiz stave from his pack as a walking stick.  He walked from the camp, towards the ice river again. “You can mail the message to Ortallius in the South Desert of Ro.  But I’ll be working with Lon for awhile I imagine.”
<br />

<br />
	Cemberfrost nodded solemnly and Fubarz waved Snide goodbye, wishing him the blessing of Tunare on his quest.
<br />

<br />

<br />
<span style="font-style: italic">Hopefully this isn't too offbase, I've been trying to get in contact with you for some time, Fubarz. Hope you like the drawing, although its been some time since I've seen you, I forget if you have a beard or not.  *scratches head*</span></span><span class="gensmall"></span></td>
